  "stem": "For \\(x > 0\\), the expression \\(\\sqrt{18x} \\cdot \\sqrt{2x^{3}}\\) is equivalent to \\(kx^{2}\\), where \\(k\\) is a constant. What is the value of \\(k\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "6"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Multiply under one radical: \\(\\sqrt{18x \\cdot 2x^{3}} = \\sqrt{36x^{4}}\\).",
    "\\(\\sqrt{36x^{4}} = 6x^{2}\\), so \\(k = 6\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x', positive=True)\nk = simplify(sqrt(18*x)*sqrt(2*x**3)/x**2)\nassert k == 6\nassert [Rational(v) for v in spr_answers] == [k]",
